      ],
      "short": "A polished Coalition official from Sur-la-Clef whom you meet in apartment #28, home of the Smoker on the Balcony; he may have seen something on the night of the hanging.",
      "details": "He introduces himself as Charles Villedrouin, an official of the Coalition Government working for the 'Institute of Price Stabilité'. He is eager to explain inflation targets, EPIS and the benefits of peace and prosperity, and stresses that he is only in Martinaise unofficially.\n\nHe speaks warmly but vaguely of his young 'friend', and you may run into him again strolling on the coast.",
      "spoiler": "He saw part of the night's events from the balcony: around half past midnight a group of men carried what looked like a body into the yard while the surrounding windows went dark. He never saw the hanging itself or heard any shots.",
