      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "The Whirling-in-Rags' former waitress, who quit just before you woke up; you can reach her on the radio and hear exactly how badly you behaved.",
      "details": "She left because of the rotting body in the yard, an awkward moment with Garte, and above all your drunken antics: waving your gun and badge around, smashing a stuffed skua, wrecking your room, clogging the toilet with police documents and singing the same sad song over and over.\n\nShe is nervous on the line, mostly worried about getting in trouble with the Union, and would rather you never called again.",
      "spoiler": "She actually liked Garte and was flattered when he asked for her number; she asks you to tell him she is sorry.",
