    {
      "id": "the-gardener",
      "term": "The Gardener",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A polite young woman with a wheelbarrow at the corner by the Whirling-in-Rags; she gives directions and can lend you gloves and smelling salts.",
      "details": "She says she is working on the gardens by the yard but keeps taking breaks because of the smell of the corpse. Ask her for directions around Martinaise, borrow her rubber gloves for the autopsy, or get ammonia salts for the stench. She mentions that the Wild Pines company woman is in town.",
      "spoiler": "She is not a gardener: she is Elizabeth 'Lizzie' Beaufort, a legal counsellor for the Dockworkers' Union (Evrart paid for her schooling) who has been keeping an eye on you, and she reappears at the Whirling to steer you towards Titus. She is badly hurt if the tribunal turns violent.",
