    {
      "id": "the-pigs",
      "term": "The Pigs",
      "aliases": [
        "Auntie LePlante",
        "Marianne LePlante",
        "Miss LePlante"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A confused old woman who haunts the old fish market on the boardwalk at night, buried in scavenged police gear and yelling police jargon through a megaphone.",
      "details": "She calls herself 'the Pigs' and is convinced she is a police officer. She wears a mountain of RCM paraphernalia with battery-powered sirens and beacon lights strapped to her back, barely registers the people around her, and keeps calling out for a 'Mr. Morrand'.",
      "spoiler": "She has your missing service pistol: Evrart Claire arranges for you to meet her at the old fish market at night, where she points the three-barrelled gun at you; it turns out to be unloaded. Afterwards you can ask the Hardie Boys to look after her. Titus remembers her as 'Auntie LePlante' (Marianne LePlante), an old woman who did right by the dockworkers when they were kids; her own children moved away and never visit. 'Mr. Morrand' is Gareth Morrand, a former cop turned crime-show host on Channel 8 radio.",
      "seeAlso": [
