      "term": "Theo",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "commonWord": true,
      "short": "The oldest and quietest of the Hardie Boys: a silver-haired dockworker in his fifties who smokes and watches from the back of their room at the Whirling.",
      "details": "Theo speaks slowly and rarely, and when he does it is blunt. He has a grim bet running that you will end up killing yourself, and says so in an almost kind voice. Like Eugene, he is of Areopagite descent.\n\nIf you are after the spare workshop key, he can fetch it from the tree outside the window and slide it across the table, while insisting he couldn't care less about your key.",
      "spoiler": "Theo can be among the Hardie Boys killed in the shootout at the tribunal; Kim remarks that he was simply too old for that kind of fight.",
