    {
      "id": "tiago",
      "term": "Tiago",
      "aliases": [
        "crab-man",
        "Crab Man"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "commonWord": true,
      "short": "A wiry man who lives in the rafters of the old church, carving wooden figures and urging you to give up drink for the love of 'the Mother'.",
      "details": "The speedfreaks camped outside call him the crab-man because of the way he scuttles along the beams; he prefers to think of himself as a flame. He is Mesque and speaks in Mesque slang. He says he was once in a gang and a heavy drinker, but his memories of that life are fading, which he sees as a blessing.\n\nHe calls himself a saeraff who sings the silent glory of the Mother of Silence, and he keeps telling you that the bottle is wrecking your mind and spirit.",
      "spoiler": "He tells you there is a perforation in the world up near the church ceiling, a way out into nothingness, and that the church was built around it. He circles it, hoping to become pure enough to drink from it one day. He also knows the password to the radiocomputer of the programmer working in the church.",
      "seeAlso": [
        "church"
      ]
