    {
      "id": "tommy-le-homme",
      "term": "Tommy Le Homme",
      "aliases": [
        "Tommy",
        "Jerry Lefitte"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "commonWord": true,
      "short": "A lorry driver stuck for a week in the traffic jam outside the harbour gates; he passes the time writing rhymes and missing his family.",
      "details": "Tommy hauls FALN sportswear (mostly tracksuits) and has to guard his cargo while the strike keeps the gates shut. He wants to become a musician, half-spoken verse over beats, and warms to you if you show some poetic talent. 'Tommy Le Homme' is a stage name; his real name is Jerry Lefitte.\n\nHis wife and child, with a second on the way, live in Deora-of-the-Seven-Seas on the island of Laurentide, at the far end of Le Caillou. He used to take drugs but says he has been clean for some time. He is friends with the 'lady driver' whose lorry stands abandoned in the jam.",
      "spoiler": "The lady driver left him the keys to her lorry before she disappeared. He insists she is no drug trafficker and would rather not help you find her.",
      "seeAlso": [
        "strike",
        "harbour"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trant-heidelstam",
      "term": "Trant Heidelstam",
      "aliases": [
        "Trant"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A friendly, endlessly knowledgeable man you meet on the boardwalk with his young son, eager to explain the hidden history of West Martinaise.",
      "details": "Trant is showing his son Mikael the ruined Feld Electrical building by the big mural. He explains that Feld built this side of Martinaise as a research centre during the turn-of-the-century cybernetics boom, and that the Coalition landed here in '08. He has something to say about almost everything, from tape computers and the Commune's March decree to Lo Manthang stick fighting, which he has practised for nearly twenty years.\n\nHe is pleasant company but lectures until you doze off. One of his asides can give you a Thought.",
      "spoiler": "He turns up again at the very end of the case as a special consultant brought in by the RCM, offering theories about your amnesia and very interested in the public-relations value of what you have found.",
      "seeAlso": [
        "mikael-heidelstam",
        "coalition",
        "commune",
        "rcm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ulixes",
      "term": "Ulixes",
      "aliases": [
        "Uli",
        "Comrade Ulixes"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "Steban's sidekick in the communist reading group at the Capeside Apartments, nicknamed Uli. He echoes and backs up whatever Steban says.",
      "details": "He is the one member of the reading group whom Steban has not excommunicated, and the game simply labels him the Echo Maker: an intellectual hanger-on who repeats Steban's points, sometimes to Steban's irritation. Steban says Uli's father is from Gottwald and that Ulixes is especially interested in capitalist violence.\n\nThe two students argue theory, test how much 'plasm' they can muster between them, and play board games such as one about managing your own Zone of Ecological Catastrophe. Cindy the SKULL knows them both.",
      "spoiler": "The bylines in the student zine La Fumée look like pseudonyms; Logic suspects they are anagrams of Steban and Ulixes.",
      "seeAlso": [
