      "id": "women-s-rights",
      "term": "Women's Rights",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A lone protester with a women's rights sign standing among the strikebreakers at the harbour gates, possibly at the wrong protest.",
      "details": "The protester chants for equal wages, against domestic abuse and against being told to smile, and at one point wonders aloud whether this is the correct protest.",
      "inspiredBy": "The drunken mutterings you can hear later paraphrase Valerie Solanas's SCUM Manifesto (1967).",
      "spoiler": "Later in the game the protester can be found lying drunk in the sand on the coast, mumbling anti-male slogans.",
