      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A tired woman browsing the soggy books at the book stand on the plaza; she insists her husband and daughters are not missing.",
      "details": "She would rather read than talk to the police. Her daughters, she says, are safe at a party in Jamrock, and her husband went to the library yesterday morning to fetch her a book, promising to come straight home. Pushing her on it only irritates her.",
      "spoiler": "She is Billie Méjean, and her husband Victor is the dead man found on the Martinaise boardwalk. You can end up breaking the news to her at her flat in the apartment building.",
